From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Jun 2026 22:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] nvme/pci: prefer asynchronous probe

Move nvme_driver probe off the main init thread by setting
PROBE_PREFER_ASYNCHRONOUS on its embedded device_driver.  The NVMe
device is the Lumen rootfs device, but the kernel cmdline already
contains "rootwait", so the VFS will block until nvme0n1 appears
regardless of probe order.  Moving the probe async lets other bus
devices enumerate in parallel, reducing the critical-path length to
root-mount.

The .driver sub-struct was previously guarded by #ifdef CONFIG_PM_SLEEP,
which made it absent on non-PM builds.  Restructure to always emit
.driver with probe_type unconditionally and keep .pm inside the ifdef.

Reference:
https://docs.nvidia.com/jetson/archives/r35.6.2/DeveloperGuide/SD/Kernel/KernelBootTimeOptimization.html#asynchronous-probe

Signed-off-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/nvme/host/pci.c | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/nvme/host/pci.c b/drivers/nvme/host/pci.c
index 5f60a6ca..00000001 100644
--- a/drivers/nvme/host/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/nvme/host/pci.c
@@ -3499,12 +3499,13 @@ static struct pci_driver nvme_driver = {
 	.probe		= nvme_probe,
 	.remove		= nvme_remove,
 	.shutdown	= nvme_shutdown,
-#ifdef CONFIG_PM_SLEEP
 	.driver		= {
-		.pm	= &nvme_dev_pm_ops,
+#ifdef CONFIG_PM_SLEEP
+		.pm		= &nvme_dev_pm_ops,
+#endif
+		.probe_type	= PROBE_PREFER_ASYNCHRONOUS,
 	},
-#endif
 	.sriov_configure = pci_sriov_configure_simple,
 	.err_handler	= &nvme_err_handler,
 };
